BT /F2 10 Tf 40 689.0 Td (Example C: Multilateral Netting & Settlement Calculation) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 676.0 Td (**Scenario:** End of Month settlement between 3 group companies:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 664.5 Td (\225 Company A owes Company B **$100,000**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 653.0 Td (\225 Company A owes Company C **$50,000**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 50 641.5 Td (\225 Company B owes Company C **$20,000**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 630.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 618.5 Td (Without netting, 3 separate international wire transfers are required \($170,000 total transferred\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 607.0 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 595.5 Td (1. Go to **Inter Company Netting Cycle > New**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 584.0 Td (2. Enter `Cycle Name`: *March 2026 Netting*.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 572.5 Td (3. In the Companies table, click **Fetch Outstanding Invoices**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 561.0 Td (4. The system computes Net Positions:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 549.5 Td (- **Company A:** Net Debtor: $-\\$150,000$) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 538.5 Td (- **Company B:** Net Creditor: $+\\$80,000$) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 527.5 Td (- **Company C:** Net Creditor: $+\\$70,000$) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 516.5 Td (5. Click **Calculate Netting**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 505.0 Td (6. The engine generates 2 optimized settlements:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 493.5 Td (- *Settlement 1:* Company A pays Company B **$80,000**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 482.5 Td (- *Settlement 2:* Company A pays Company C **$70,000**) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 471.5 Td (7. Total funds wired reduced to **$150,000** \(a $20,000 liquidity saving and elimination of cross-border banking fees\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 460.0 Td (8. Click **Generate Settlement Journal Entries** to post balancing GL records across all 3 ledgers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 448.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F2 10 Tf 40 437.0 Td (Example D: Raising and Resolving a Billing Dispute) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 424.0 Td (**Scenario:** Company B was billed $1,500 on Sales Invoice `SINV-00100`, but received damaged items worth $300.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 412.5 Td () Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 401.0 Td (1. Open `SINV-00100`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 389.5 Td (2. Under the top menu, click **Inter Company > Raise Dispute**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 378.0 Td (3. In the new `Inter Company Dispute` document:) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 366.5 Td (- `Source Amount`: $1,500) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 355.5 Td (- `Target Amount`: $1,200) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 344.5 Td (- `Variance Amount`: $300 \(calculated automatically\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 65 333.5 Td (- `Dispute Reason`: *Damaged Goods*) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 322.5 Td (4. Set status to `Under Investigation`.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 311.0 Td (5. Under Resolution Action, select: `Issue Credit Note` for $300.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 299.5 Td (6. Click **Execute Resolution**.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 288.0 Td (7. The system creates and links a Credit Note return invoice in the seller entity and updates the intercompany variance to zero.) Tj ET
BT /F1 8.5 Tf 40 276.5 Td () Tj ET
